From: hottestad1 <hottestad1@bloomberg.net>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 14:40:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] GH-0000 Let the LMDB native type-matrix kernel honour
 query cancellation

LmdbNativeTypeMatrix only polled the probe deadline, which is unset in normal
execution, so a query timeout, client disconnect or close never stopped a
running type-matrix scan; serial scans always ran to completion.

The group step now passes its NativeCancellationToken to the type matrix,
which enters it for the scan and polls it alongside every probe-deadline poll
(amortised to every 1024 ticks, the probe poll's own mask). Parallel workers
enter the same token and also check it once per claimed morsel or range; a
cancellation propagates as KernelQueryCancelledException without triggering a
fallback strategy.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
